  "limitations": [
    "Single-view TRELLIS reconstruction from one approved concept: the far side, back and underside are TRELLIS's invention, with no rear-view painting projected onto them.",
    "Roughness, metalness and ambient occlusion are derived from colour classes and Cycles bakes, not measured PBR or hand-painted masks.",
    "Re-cooking is not guaranteed to be byte-reproducible: MikkTSpace tangents can round differently on a few vertices.",
    "The tower is hollow with a black interior (not visible from the gameplay camera); icicles and basket bars are soft and partly fused, and the logs are frosted grey rather than split wood.",
    "Ice is a colour class (roughness 0.22), not a refractive or subsurface material; snow and ice are painted, not simulated.",
    "Placed at 0.98 of the 2.8 m building reach, the tower stands 17.9 m at all three buildings, where the procedural beacon stood 13.4, 15.5 and 17.5 m on its 13, 15 and 17 m buildings; at the closest camera its top leaves the frame. The blockers are unchanged.",
    "Maps ship GPU-compressed as Basis Universal UASTC in KTX2 (ktx2_glb.py; about a quarter of the video memory of decoded WebP): against the cooked maps the transcoded result measures 39.7 to 42.6 dB PSNR at full size and 35.1 to 40.0 dB at a quarter size (what the game camera samples), so close-ups can show faint 4x4 block artefacts."
  ]
